Done. Experiment 121 implements **FP8 matmuls** via `torch._scaled_mm` with a custom autograd function (`_Float8Matmul`), applied to all 48 linear layers per forward pass (MLP c_fc/c_proj + attention c_q/c_k/c_v/c_proj). This is the "more steps" strategy that worked so well with MLP 3x (-0.008), but via 2x faster matmuls instead of smaller matrices. Main risk is crash from API incompatibility with torch.compile.
